        "kajVemo": [
          "The Allied airlift over Krasinec took place over two nights, specifically on 25–26 March 1945. In this operation, Allied Dakotas and Spitfires flew 2041 people from the partisan airfield of Krasinec, including wounded individuals, children, and Allied airmen. Among the evacuees was the writer Alma Karlin. [[zracni-most-krasinec]]",
          "The event occurred at the end of March 1945, during which Allied aircraft evacuated wounded Partisans from Bela krajina to Bari. Two photographs taken at Griblje document this operation. [[evakuacija-1945]]"
